# ---- B2521 (S6-B2520k): a tracked-status audit, decided per GROUP.
# The council was unanimous that the split was accidental, not a policy:
# 31 per-cube result JSONs are tracked and ~39 identical siblings were not,
# so a citation resolved for the author and not for a reader. Those are
# EVIDENCE and are now tracked. What follows is DERIVED - regenerable from
# code plus inputs - so it is ignored rather than stored.
# Regeneration: scripts/build_institutional_persistence.py (per parameter set).
data_prefetch/derived/institutional_persistence_t1a_*/
# scratch probes written during a turn; never evidence, never cited.
output_audit/_*

# B2529 EXCEPTION to the output_audit/_* scratch rule above. These two are
# NOT scratch: the .cmd IS the launch payload a running Task Scheduler task
# executes, and the .json is the launch record the queue row cites. The rule
# is right and the filenames were wrong; renaming them while the task holds
# the path is the riskier fix, so the exception is recorded here where a
# reader will find it (#279 - an exclusion you cannot see is a fail-open).
!output_audit/_b2527_chain.cmd
!output_audit/_b2527_chain_task.json
